            <ArticleTitle>The cognitive-emotional brain: Opportunities [corrected] and challenges for understanding neuropsychiatric disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S0140525X14001010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many of the most common neuropsychiatric disorders are marked by prominent disturbances of cognition and emotion. Characterizing the complex neural circuitry underlying the interplay of cognition and emotion is critically important, not just for clarifying the nature of the mind, but also for discovering the root causes of a broad spectrum of debilitating neuropsychiatric disorders, including anxiety, schizophrenia, and chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
